qmd 2.5.3: resolve vector matches by content hash, read bodies last

searchVec resolved its KNN matches with
`WHERE cv.hash || '_' || cv.seq IN (...)`, which cannot use the
(hash, seq) primary key of content_vectors and scans every chunk row,
and it read the full body of every matching document. The lookup now
goes by `cv.hash IN (unique hashes)` and keeps the matched seqs in JS;
bodies are read only for the results returned. Same rows, same order.

Applies to the published package (dist/) with `patch -p1` from the
package root.

